397 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (1. Mindfulness and Meditation: Practice mindfulness to stay present and reduce anxiety. Meditation can also help calm the mind.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [22]
>>
endobj
398 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (2. Regular Exercise: Physical activity can reduce stress hormones and increase endorphins, which are natural mood lifters.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [23]
>>
endobj
399 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (3. Healthy Diet: Eating a balanced diet can support your mental health. Avoid excessive caffeine and sugar, which can increase anxiety.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [24]
>>
endobj
400 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (4. Adequate Sleep: Ensure you get enough restful sleep, as lack of sleep can contribute to stress and anxiety.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [25]
>>
endobj
401 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (5. Stress Management Techniques: Explore techniques such as deep breathing, progressive muscle relaxation, or yoga to manage stress.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [26]
>>
endobj
402 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (6. Social Support: Talk to friends or family about your feelings. Sharing your thoughts can help reduce stress.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [27]
>>
endobj
403 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (7. Time Management: Prioritize tasks and set realistic goals to reduce feelings of being overwhelmed.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [28]
>>
endobj
404 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (8. Limit Stressors: Identify sources of stress and try to minimize or avoid them when possible.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [29]
>>
endobj
405 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (9. Seek Professional Help: If stress becomes overwhelming, consider talking to a mental health professional for guidance and support.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [30]
>>
endobj
